SELECT 21, 'medium', '[Amazon SDE PYQ] What is the average time complexity of finding the Lowest Common Ancestor (LCA) of two nodes in a balanced Binary Search Tree (BST) of N nodes?', NULL, 'dsa', 'O(1)', 'O(log N)', 'O(N)', 'O(N log N)', 'B', 'In a balanced Binary Search Tree (BST), the height is O(log N). Starting from the root, we compare both node values: if both are smaller, we move to the left child; if both are larger, we move to the right child; otherwise, the current node is the Lowest Common Ancestor (LCA). At most O(h) = O(log N) comparisons are made (Option B).', 60, 'Amazon SDE PYQ', 1, 'verified_pyq', 'verified', 'Amazon', SHA1('[Amazon SDE PYQ] What is the average time complexity of finding the Lowest Common Ancestor (LCA) of two nodes in a balanced Binary Search Tree (BST) of N nodes?')
